    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theming.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Theming, split on the stage it fails at",
      "prov:value": "**Every file here is named for the skill it declares, and that is load-bearing\nrather than tidy.** `servableSkills()` in `scripts/kg-audit.ts` derives a\nskill's id from its FILENAME, while `package-manifest.json` lists its `name:` —\nso a file whose basename differs from its `name:` is declared, present, and\nreported as `manifest-skill-exists` because the two sides never meet. Measured\nhere on the first pass: six criticals, from six files named for their stage\ninstead of for their skill."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theming.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Theming, split on the stage it fails at",
      "prov:value": "**This is a PACKAGE under `skills/`, not a top-level declared directory**, and\nthe difference was paid for. Two sessions built this package independently on\n2026-09-20: one relocated `theme-art-intake`, `create-sticky-note` and\n`site-presentation-assets` out of folio-core into `skills/ui/theming/`; the other\nwrote the stage split, the visualiser and the documentation entry into a\ntop-level `cat-harness/theming/`. The merge kept both halves and took THIS\nlocation on evidence — bean `lps0` measured that `kg-audit`'s `skillFiles()`\nwalks a hardcoded `skills/`, so a top-level topical directory silently drops\nits skills out of skill QA, and `theme-art-intake` would have lost the sidecar\nit has here.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean lps0",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theming.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The axis, and the ordering matters more than the names",
      "prov:value": "The owner, 2026-09-20, asked for theming skills *\"broken up thematically\"* and\nthen chose the axis: **\"1 + 2, then specialized to 3\"** — three levels, not a\nchoice between three options.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theming.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The axis, and the ordering matters more than the names",
      "prov:value": "**Stage is primary because that is how the failures actually arrive.** Four\nrounds of *\"still not image\"* were one cause, and each round was one stage."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theming.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why this directory exists at all",
      "prov:value": "Theming was spread across places that do not name themselves as theming:\n`schemas/ui/themes.ts`, `schemas/ui/theme.ts`, `schemas/content/landing-sticky.ts`, the\ngenerated `docs-ui.css`, `themes:css`, `check:theme-art`, the scrim measurement\nrules and the avatar crop boxes — with the discipline recorded in one skill's\nprose and nowhere else. Bean `1hvo`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 1hvo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/theming/theming.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Looking at it",
      "prov:value": "`bun run cat theme:sheet` renders every theme — palette, measured contrast, and\neach layout's art with its `textRegion` and `avatarRegion` drawn. It PRINTS and\nnever gates, because the question it answers is one no assertion can carry: the\nschema can prove a box is square and inside the frame, and a box that is both\nand still frames a patch of sky is exactly how two of the first seven avatar\ncrops shipped."
    }
  ]
}
